    "body": "> Out of curiosity, [@jakearchibald](https://github.com/jakearchibald) does your PR rely on appending things mid-iteration and then also iterating over them later in the same for-each loop? Because the JS model would break that I believe.\n\nI'm only 3+ years late with this reply…\n\n```js\nconst arr = [1, 2];\n\nfor (const val of arr) {\n  console.log(val);\n  \n  if (val === 1) arr.push(3);\n}\n```\n\nThe above logs 1, 2, 3.\n\nI tend to use this technique in breadth-first iteration since the deeper steps are pushed to the end.",
